<title>POLAND: Polish NBP buys dollars at PLN 3.2200 - dealers.</title>
<headline>Polish NBP buys dollars at PLN 3.2200 - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland (NBP) again bought dollars on the interbank market, this time at 3.2200 zlotys, dealers said.</p>
<p>The intervention, described as &quot;medium&quot; in quantity, came at 1215 GMT when the zloty was at 1.50 percent from the dollar/mark parity rate for today.</p>
<p>Earlier the NBP also repeatedly bought dollars between 3.2192 and 3.2195 zlotys and marks at 1.8799 and 1.8800.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
